Project Development Phase

ComicCraft-AI – Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models

The Project Development Phase is the stage where the planned design of ComicCraft-AI is converted into a working application. During this phase, the frontend, backend, database, and Gemini AI integration are developed and connected.

1. Frontend Development

The user interface is developed to make comic creation simple and interactive.

Main screens include:

Home Page – Introduction and project creation options.

Story Input Page – User enters story idea, genre, characters, and setting.

Generation Page – Displays AI generation progress.

Comic Preview Page – Shows the generated story as comic panels.

Edit Page – Allows users to modify stories and dialogues.

Save/Export Page – Allows users to save or export their comic.


2. Backend Development

The backend manages communication between the user interface, database, and Gemini models.

Main functions:

Receive user inputs.

Validate the entered information.

Create prompts for Gemini.

Send requests to the Gemini API.

Receive and process AI-generated responses.

Store comic projects.

Send generated content back to the frontend.


3. Gemini AI Integration

Gemini models are integrated as the main AI component of ComicCraft-AI.

The system sends structured prompts such as:

> "Create a 6-panel superhero comic story. Include a title, characters, scene descriptions, dialogues, and captions."



Gemini generates the required content, which is then processed and displayed by the application.

4. Story Generation Module

The story generation module converts a user's basic idea into a complete comic story.

It generates:

Comic title

Story summary

Beginning, middle, and ending

Characters

Scenes

Dialogues

Captions

Panel descriptions


5. Character Generation Module

This module creates detailed character information, including:

Character name

Age

Personality

Appearance

Role in the story

Character relationships


This information helps maintain consistency throughout the comic.

6. Comic Panel Generation

The generated story is divided into individual panels.

Each panel contains:

Component	Description

Panel Number	Identifies the panel
Scene	Describes what happens
Character	Characters appearing in the scene
Dialogue	Character speech
Caption	Narration or additional information
Image Prompt	Description for creating the visual


7. Database Development

A database is used to store:

User information

Comic projects

Story content

Character details

Comic panels

Generated prompts

Saved versions


This allows users to access and edit their comics later.

8. Testing During Development

Each module is tested individually and then tested together.

Testing includes:

Unit Testing – Tests individual functions.

Integration Testing – Tests frontend, backend, database, and Gemini integration.

UI Testing – Checks buttons, forms, navigation, and display.

AI Output Testing – Checks whether generated stories are relevant and consistent.

Error Testing – Checks API failures, invalid inputs, and network problems.


